# LAMMPS input for backmapping — generated by backmap-prep, hand-tuned to the
# original 2016/2018 ESPResSo++ protocol (see notebook
# 2026-07-12_at-intrabead-always-on-fix.md for why the CG-frozen/AT-relax
# "Phase 0a/0b" approach was dropped, and why AT atoms do NOT need to be
# frozen during the lambda=0 equilibration below):
#   Phase 0 — minimize the whole hybrid structure at lambda=0. AT intra-bead
#             (same CG bead / same-molecule) bonded and nonbonded terms are
#             ALWAYS fully active, independent of lambda (real
#             intra-molecular chemistry — see docs/theory.md); only
#             inter-bead (intermolecular) AT-AT terms and CG-CG terms are
#             lambda-dependent, and CG-CG is at full strength at lambda=0.
#             So minimizing at lambda=0 relaxes both the CG structure and
#             each fragment's local AT geometry.
#   Phase 1 — CG equilibration at lambda=0 (real thermalized dynamics for
#             both CG and AT — this is the "CG equilibration (lambda=0)"
#             step of the original protocol; AT atoms are thermalized too
#             since their intra-bead chemistry gives them real restoring
#             forces, matching the original ESPResSo++ driver
#             bakery/src/start_backmapping.py, which thermostats AT
#             particles throughout with a single constant-gamma Langevin
#             thermostat).
#   Phase 2 — lambda ramp. Fix backmap becomes active and drives the CG bead
#             position via COM-shift toward the AT center of mass (not by
#             independent CG force integration); inter-bead AT-AT and CG-CG
#             terms fade in/out with lambda.
#   Phase 3 — AT production at lambda=1 (fix backmap stays active, pinned at
#             lambda=1 once the ramp saturates).
# Reference: Krajniak et al., JCTC 2016, DOI: 10.1021/acs.jctc.6b00595
#            Krajniak, Zhang et al., JCC 2018, DOI: 10.1002/jcc.25129
#
# Phase step counts default to a short pilot (a few ps each); override with
# -var NAME VALUE on the command line for the full ~1 ns eq-at-lambda=0 /
# ~1 ns production-at-lambda=1 run, e.g.:
#   mpirun -np 8 lmp -in in.pet \
#     -var eq0_steps 1000000 -var ramp_steps 10000 \
#     -var prod_steps_a 2000 -var prod_steps_b 2000 -var prod_steps_c 998000

# "index"-style variables are no-ops if already set by -var on the command
# line, so these are just the pilot defaults.
variable eq0_steps index 5000
variable ramp_steps index 10000
variable prod_steps_a index 2000
variable prod_steps_b index 2000
variable prod_steps_c index 5000

units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p

read_data pet.data
reset_atoms image all

comm_modify cutoff 75.00

pair_style backmap 12.00 lj/cut/coul/cut 12.00 9.00 14.00 table linear 1000
